\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Overall ending structure\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 The climax consists of several 
\f1\b \strokec2 parallel confrontations
\f2\b0 \strokec2 , all converging during the final minutes before sunrise. None receives a normal resolution. Each is cut off a hair's breadth before resolution by the recurring terminal line:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 And that's when Sarah's waters broke.
\f2\b0 \strokec2 \
Sarah's waters breaking signals the final event: the Dawkins ascends and the universe ends. The abruptness is deliberate.\
The current Aeon design places the principal final threads roughly between 
\f1\b \strokec2 05:32 and 05:42
\f2\b0 \strokec2 , with 
\f3\fs26 \strokec2 Birth of the Dawkins
\f2\fs24 \strokec2  at 
\f1\b \strokec2 05:42
\f2\b0 \strokec2 . Aeon is useful here as narrative design, while individual timings remain adjustable when newer drafting requires it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

