\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::1>
\f1\b\fs48 Fridge Force\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::1><$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Institutional facts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 Fridge Force is a 
\f1\b \strokec2 government agency
\f2\b0 \strokec2 .\
Its overt role is maintaining/regulating stasis-unit applications and guarding the technology extraordinarily jealously. The novel has repeatedly established fear of Fridge Force and extreme consequences for tampering with stasis technology.\
The climax reveals that its capabilities go much deeper than most characters\'97or the reader\'97have previously seen.\
The drone display includes the familiar warning about tampering invalidating 
\f1\b \strokec2 the warranty of your life
\f2\b0 \strokec2 , so the reveal is surprising without being arbitrary.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Fridge Force's objectives\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 Its principal objectives are:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 A. Recover the stolen Gyges discs.
\f2\b0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 
\f1\b \strokec2 B. Shut Project Kebab down.
\f2\b0 \strokec2 \
Its operational consequence is effectively:\

\f1\b \strokec2 C. Neutralise anything capable of obstructing A or B.
\f2\b0 \strokec2 \
The prose should 
\f1\b \strokec2 show those objectives through behaviour
\f2\b0 \strokec2 , rather than explaining them as a mission statement.\
So the UDF need not commit some special moral offence against Fridge Force. Its weapons, checkpoints, anti-air capability, command positions and other equipment are simply 
\f1\b \strokec2 obstacles capable of preventing Fridge Force from completing its operation
\f2\b0 \strokec2 .\
That is sufficient reason for MoSES to neutralise them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

